{"title":"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> has center on the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_quadrilateral\" title=\"Cyclic quadrilateral\">cyclic quadrilateral</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.  The other three sides are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent\" title=\"Tangent\">tangent</a> to the circle.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5e35daf09d12b065ceddb37704dc5aef9d3f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD + BC = AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the circle mentioned in the problem.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the second intersection of the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/730567da5509f1137eb7015905644110979b897f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDO$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.  By measures of arcs, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a8d008ef568621ca5766ff8a4cd20697f42eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DTA = \\angle DCO = \\frac{\\angle DCB}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\angle DAB}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"342\" height=\"38\" />.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff78bf4a70fb0008f807b627039f888c77f5e61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AT = AD$\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />.  Likewise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09ec570a0e4ab0b1abd30ce60e740c4e18d49d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TB = BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5e35daf09d12b065ceddb37704dc5aef9d3f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD + BC = AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />, as desired.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the circle mentioned in the problem, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff78bf4a70fb0008f807b627039f888c77f5e61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AT = AD$\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/28200a53ac997a848407f89311e78e75fecbcac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DTA = \\frac{ \\pi - \\angle DAB}{2} = \\angle DCO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"254\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/300fce675f32372d72b8412ec905e7a5727eeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DCOT$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is in fact the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of the previous solution.  The conclusion follows.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the circle have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and let its points of tangency with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36d309e06ef6e81fc451ca227569ca1799a0e42f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, CD, DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84fa54f1f4c06247f291d06bbac485b2a72b086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, F, G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />, respectively.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/418acda559404764a2e375718c40b812eb6b0b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEFC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is clearly a cyclic quadrilateral, the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca99f32c7775b5fc0252d751d588bbac96ba4357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to half the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aacc89aed81f195af5c17472a2a174e11db04d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GAO$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.  Then\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f3c64cee1ffd738163a33061ea229386b81013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} {CE} &amp; = &amp; r \\tan(COE) \\\\ &amp; = &amp;r \\left( \\frac{1 - \\cos (GAO)}{\\sin(GAO)} \\right) \\\\ &amp; = &amp; AO - AG \\\\ \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"186\" height=\"65\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Likewise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba00eb362071f7fe243d2caf3f3ed8db0a6518a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG = OB - EB$\" width=\"134\" height=\"12\" />.  It follows that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/106c15de77b3d722e4b5d9d4cea0464618d1954c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${EB} + CE + DG + GA = AO + OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"288\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We use the notation of the previous solution.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on the ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb81b5b411fb12220c9a489e68fb2afb0f5eecca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = AO$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />.  We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d434c2046737968df55b03efe5ba872a4522f13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OF = OG = r$\" width=\"113\" height=\"12\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4398d6dfc0b87c8f52ddb0cf634a83e247348b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OFC = \\angle OGX = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"33\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc6fcbaaf711b26c9779291610ac3f89b089babe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FCO = \\angle GXO = \\frac{\\pi - \\angle BAD}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"254\" height=\"38\" />; hence the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e8e24d8ccb4a85ae3e769b2b36fd2d211339a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OFC, OGX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> are congruent; hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e019e4f1093cd38cd1df2de6eef39c6715b34d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GX = FC = CE$\" width=\"136\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea24a691b8a68f3d2339bb01b0598b8ceac9af6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO = AG + GX = AG + CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"236\" height=\"14\" />.  Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c4544b99a4a8a1d691f2e21918d4518de49f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB = EB + GD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92f22c6953049b4f36e2ff6923b7c64796c3450a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO + OB = AG + GD + CE + EB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"285\" height=\"14\" />, Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>This solution is incorrect. The fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circle does not necessitate that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is its point of tangency. -Nitinjan06\n</p><p>From the fact that AD and BC are tangents to the circle mentioned in the problem, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e66ab5e048aef5c6bb9283f53f3aae74f5aeba57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBA}=90\\deg$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b768f225273939554387b77d2762d6efe3bc6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAB}=90\\deg$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now, from the fact that ABCD is cyclic, we obtain that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e02277a9335c294ccfd8f0b574f357b250d0558a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BCD}=90\\deg$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/69170828e5986b00fe03e26197b20056aa9dee0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CDA}=90\\deg$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />,\nsuch that ABCD is a rectangle.\n</p><p>Now, let E be the point of tangency between the circle and CD. It follows, if O is the center of the circle, that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16336db6649ec3a1833fd19ee9339cfbd954fa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{OEC}=\\angle{OED}=90\\deg$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"210\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7e6820264dba2d41e966b96192a82756f0fd39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO=EO=BO$\" width=\"133\" height=\"13\" />, we obtain two squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc80036a370108e315e1194a3a7b556103f6850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOED$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078bdee22d0a535d3a24f6dcbd172f3f7fb5c22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOEC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />.\nFrom the properties of squares we now have\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bc265b889c5fb58337a14803f82b9bfcc1fd75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD+BC=AO+BO=AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"235\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\nas desired.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Lemma. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the in-center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be on the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/80080eae22690988d278d9843059f70c78ff45f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP + CQ = BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9418fbdd63cdaf19a108382fd5617783a92cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APIQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral.\n</p><p>Solution. Assume that rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the center od circle touching <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Obviosuly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-ex-center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dde9d165bd0be8919e9c7d40e4e750c2eeaeb74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PDB$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a732aec25230c4c7b93d7c870efe6e0ed63e70c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DSI=\\angle DSP = \\frac{1}{2} \\angle DCP=\\frac{1}{2} \\angle A=\\angle DAI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"365\" height=\"38\" /> so DASI is concyclic.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_2\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tM0WhXNCWGU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tM0WhXNCWGU</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ormv0y4ZM1E\">https://youtu.be/Ormv0y4ZM1E</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175229\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 414/1000000\nPost‐expand include siz